Thursday-Friday
basically Just got settled Into the apartment and did media missionary work
for most the week not gonna lie, weren't any lessons or activities =F0=9F=
=91=BB

Saturday
Went to a member's mother=E2=80=99s funeral ceremony, was very interesting =
how
everything is done in Japan compared with America. Was a bit sad, but I
trust that she's overlooking us in a better place.
Afterwards we got some Katsu Curry Udon, which was incredibly tasty. Loved
it. =F0=9F=98=A2=F0=9F=98=8A

Sunday
Today I had my first sacrament Meeting in Marugame! It was great! I gave a
short testimony near the start of the meeting, which was fun. Later that
day we went over to a members house to celebrate Ogita=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9Fs b=
irthday! It was
super fun even though I don't know if I've ever Actually talked to him =F0=
=9F=98=82
The sisters were also there, we played a bunch of games, was so fun lol.

Pday
Lots of shopping for stuff, did a couple madlibs with my family over zoom
which was super funny. A member took us put to get Ramen (I ate only Gyoza
and ice cream lol) and afterwards took us out to buy groceries for the next
week, was super nice =E2=9D=A4=EF=B8=8F

Sorry this email wasn=E2=80=99t very long, the week low key was cut short f=
rom the
get-go lol. Gotta balance out the extra long email I guess.

Spiritual thought!
Think about how you'd feel if you worked really hard on a gift for someone
you cared about, only to have them open it, frown, and throw the box and
the gift away. That's a pretty sucky feeling, right? I think it's kind of
similar to our lives and our relationship with God. He is our loving
Heavenly Father, and has carefully prepared our bodies, and life
experiences for our own eternal benefit, and often we are far to hasty to
throw it all away. We do that in a lot of ways, but I'd encourage you to
think about what you may be doing to =E2=80=9Cthrow away that gift=E2=80=9D=
 even in simple
ways, and strive to grow and change! Fortunately, even when we make
mistakes, we are loved, and God always has our back. Jesus does too :)

Love you guys!! Hope to hear from you all when you get time =F0=9F=98=84 So=
rry I
haven't dished out a lot of responses, I will try to get on that next week!
Bye!!

=E3=82=AD=E3=83=AA=E3=82=A2=E3=83=B3=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81

